<BaseLayout
  title="About — AndProducers"
  description="AndProducers is the modern handbook for marketing production. Practical guides, templates, and weekly articles for producers, creative ops, and marketing teams."
>
  <div class="page-header">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>About AndProducers</h1>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="container content-width" style="margin-top:var(--s-12);margin-bottom:var(--s-20)">
    <div class="prose">

      <p>AndProducers is a handbook for people who make marketing happen — producers, creative ops leads, project managers, studio heads, and anyone responsible for shipping creative at scale.</p>

      <p>Most production knowledge lives in Slack threads, tribal memory, and the heads of experienced producers who've been doing this for years. This site exists to surface it: practical guides, tested templates, real-world playbooks, and weekly articles on the craft and business of marketing production.</p>

      <h2>What you'll find here</h2>

      <p><strong>Articles</strong> — In-depth analysis and perspective on the production industry. New article every week, covering creative production ops, strategy, in-housing, martech, social, and video.</p>

      <p><strong>Guides</strong> — Evergreen how-to content that walks through how things work and how to do them well. Built to be referenced repeatedly, not just read once.</p>

      <p><strong>Templates</strong> — The actual documents and tools that production teams use: brief templates, QA checklists, content matrices, trafficking specs. All free to download, no sign-up required.</p>

      <p><strong>Playbooks</strong> — Quick SOPs for shipping safely. Designed to be shared with your team, dropped into your documentation, or printed and put on the wall.</p>

      <h2>The six pillars</h2>

      <p>Content on AndProducers is organised across six topic areas that together cover the full scope of modern marketing production:</p>

      <ul>
        <li><strong>Production Ops</strong> — Briefs, QA, trafficking, versioning, and the mechanics of shipping creative at scale.</li>
        <li><strong>Creative Strategy</strong> — Concepting, briefing, campaign architecture, and creative effectiveness.</li>
        <li><strong>In-housing</strong> — Building internal studios, managing agencies, and structuring creative ops inside brands.</li>
        <li><strong>Martech & Adtech</strong> — DCO, DAMs, CDPs, ad tech, and the tools that power modern production.</li>
        <li><strong>Social & Content</strong> — Content production for social platforms — formats, workflows, and volume production.</li>
        <li><strong>Video & Motion</strong> — Video production, motion design, editing pipelines, and broadcast-to-digital.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Implementation help</h2>

      <p>AndProducers provides the knowledge. If you need someone to deliver the work — building production infrastructure, setting up tooling, running creative ops — that's what <a href="https://productionstudio.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ProductionStudio</a> does.</p>

    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

